    "country": "United States",
    "doi": null,
    "study_design": "Randomized controlled feasibility trial; randomization process described previously, but in brief, 153 men with NIDDM were randomized into standard and intensive treatment arms. Stratification was done on the basis of clinical history of cardiovascular disease and by participating hospitals. The specific method of randomization (e.g., computer, random number table) is not detailed.",
    "inclusion_criteria": "Men with NIDDM, 40 to 69 years of age, with suboptimal glycemic control after being treated with insulin or with maximum doses of oral agents.",
    "exclusion_criteria": "Patients reporting more than 1 preexisting myocardial infarction, severe congestive heart failure (New York Heart Association class III or IV), or amputation due to gangrene were excluded. Elevated serum creatinine levels (>141.4 μmol/l [>1.6 mg/dL]), albuminuria over 500 mg/d, or symptomatic neuropathy also were exclusion criteria.",
    "study_setting": "Multicenter study conducted in 5 medical centers",
    "source_of_recruitment": "Veterans Affairs medical centers",
